[[884,351,"Lack of clinical governance of the Community Urology Service (CUS) by the Integrated Care Board (ICB) who commissioned the service and Sussex Medical Chambers (SMC) who were responsible for providing the service","lack of clinical governance of Community Urology Service",""],[885,351,"Lack of Integration of the Community Urology service with NHS Hospital Urology Services","fragmented urology service",""],[886,351,"Lack of appraisal and mandatory assessment of clinicians employed by CUS","insufficient appraisal and mandatory assessment of clinicians",""],[887,351,"Practicing Privileges within the private sector","lack of robust assessment and guidelines for practicing privileges",""],[888,351,"Learning from Mr [name redacted] death","lack of independent review of death circumstances",""],[889,351,"Management of Mr Hankin at Goring Hall Hospital","delayed sepsis diagnosis and treatment",""],[909,360,"Ms Heath was noted to be warfarin resistant and alternative medication regimes were not successful in keeping Ms Heath within a therapeutic range for her required lifelong requirement to have anticoagulation to prevent a significant risk of death","inadequate anticoagulation management",""],[910,360,"Ms Heath could not afford to fund the at home monitor as this was financially prohibitive for her being on a low income","financial barrier to monitoring",""],[911,360,"No application for funding was made on behalf of Ms Heath by the Trust nor was this explained to Ms Heath","lack of funding advocacy",""],[912,360,"There was an absence of appropriate medical records recorded for Ms Heath to understand her clinical presentation","inadequate medical documentation",""],[2459,945,"Current resources for safeguarding those with mental health illnesses whilst intoxicated may be placing people at risk","inadequate safeguarding of intoxicated individuals with mental health issues",""],[2460,945,"I heard evidence that a person who was suicidal, suffering with mental health concerns and was intoxicated could not be adequately safeguarded until he was sufficiently sober to allow a mental health assessment","delayed mental health assessment for intoxicated suicidal individuals",""]]